      "message": "Defuse both forms of command a child's report can carry\n\nThe report lands on a live parent whose gate is about to wake its agent, so\ntwo lines in the child's own words can cancel the aggregation the report\nexists to inform:\n\n- `commandLinesIn` matches `/name` AND `<!-- atomaton:dispatch=name -->` (the\n  latter through `DISPATCH_RE`, and it has no `/` in it), so escaping by\n  replacing a literal `/` left the marker intact: the thread reader saw an\n  ask nobody claimed, and the gate answered `parent-busy` and took its marker\n  back. The escape now goes in front of the character the reader starts at,\n  found by searching for the first `<` or `/` so that a list bullet keeps its\n  place.\n- `atomaton:aggregated=N` quoted in the child's report reached the gate's\n  idempotency read, which answered `already-aggregated`: no dispatch, no\n  marker, no retry. The child's text now goes through `withoutTags` before it\n  is folded in, the same reason `fetch_events` runs it on what an agent reads.\n  The body's own `llm-context` line is added afterwards and survives.\n\nTests cover both, including the hand-retyped `dispatch = name` spelling the\ntag stripper cannot see and the escape therefore has to cover alone.\n\nFull suite: 2041 pass, 0 fail. Typecheck clean.",
